CORE
main.cpp
--cpp20
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] .* unconstrained copy constructor: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] .* more constrained, other return type: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.3\] .* unsatisfied twin: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.4\] .* WRONG \(must FAIL\): FAILURE$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
--
The later twin gets its own symbol (#requires_twin); overload resolution
drops the less constrained one.  g++ 13 and clang++ 18 accept this
program, and it fails only its WRONG assertion.
